{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792519923,"nonce":"fefa/U+lJ9I6a4m5BIrg0Ad546o=","title":"TypeScript: link named and star re-exports with preserved binding identity","message":"The frontend handles local export aliases but rejects export-from and export-star declarations. Add native named/star re-exports through shared checker interfaces and compiled imports, without wrapper functions or executable body cloning.\n\nAcceptance: named renaming, transitive/diamond star forwarding, explicit exports shadow stars, distinct bindings with the same export name produce type diagnostics, and repeated paths to the same binding remain valid. Preserve type-only provenance, generic/array/release facts and initialization/elision order through source, compiled artifacts and snapshots. Extend filesystem discovery and pinned multi-file conformance. Reference execution must use the actual TypeScript checker emitter, so implicit type-only re-exports are erased correctly.\n\nNamespace export objects, default declarations, variable live bindings, cycles and persistent filesystem snapshot caching remain in parent 0c26889a7cd2c4060eb94ef93fd808c2857089dbf714735ca52b5d071bdb1564.","files":null}]}